diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..e46f447 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,65 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Payloads
+
+When an event the webhook is subscribed to happens on its board, Fizzy sends a `POST` request to the webhook's `payload_url`. Every event is delivered exactly once: deliveries are never retried, and how each one went is recorded in the delivery history above.
+
+__Request headers:__
+
+```
+User-Agent: fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook
+Content-Type: application/json
+X-Webhook-Signature: 5d41402abc4b2a76b9719d911017c592...
+X-Webhook-Timestamp: 2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z
+```
+
+`X-Webhook-Signature` is the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 digest of the request body, keyed with the webhook's `signing_secret`. Compute it on your side and compare it with the header to verify the request came from Fizzy. `X-Webhook-Timestamp` is when the event happened.
+
+Credentials embedded in the `payload_url` (`https://user:password@example.com/hooks`) are sent as HTTP basic authentication.
+
+__Request body:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde",
+  "action": "card_closed",
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+  "eventable": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohdb",
+    "number": 1,
+    "title": "Fix the logo",
+    "status": "closed",
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/cards/1"
+  },
+  "board": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy",
+    "name": "Fizzy",
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/boards/03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy"
+  },
+  "creator": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7",
+    "name": "David Heinemeier Hansson",
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/users/03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`eventable` is the full card (see [Cards](cards.md)) for `card_*` actions, and the full comment (see [Comments](comments.md)) for `comment_created`. `board` and `creator` are abbreviated above; they have the same shape as in the [Boards](boards.md) and [Users](users.md) sections.
+
+### Chat integrations
+
+Webhooks pointing at a chat service receive a human-readable message instead of the JSON payload:
+
+- __Slack__ incoming webhooks (`https://hooks.slack.com/services/...`) get `{ "text": "David moved \"Fix the logo\" to \"Done\" <url|↗︎>" }`.
+- __Campfire__ bot URLs (`https://chat.example.com/rooms/1/2-bot-key/messages`) get the message as an HTML request body with `Content-Type: text/html`.
+- __Basecamp__ chatbot URLs (`https://3.basecamp.com/1/integrations/token/buckets/2/chats/3/lines`) get `{ "content": "<html message>" }`.
+
+### Failures and deactivation
+
+A delivery succeeds when the receiver responds with a `2XX` status. Redirects are not followed, and the connection times out after 5 seconds when connecting and 10 seconds waiting for a response. Failed deliveries show up in the delivery history as `completed` with a non-`2XX` `response.code`, or as `errored` with a `response.error` of `timeout`, `ssl_error`, `destination_unreachable` or `invalid_response`.
+
+A receiver that keeps failing gets switched off: after ten failed deliveries in a row spanning at least an hour, the webhook is deactivated (`"active": false`) and stops receiving events until it is reactivated with `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks/:id/activation`. Any successful delivery resets the count.
+
+Deliveries are kept for one week.
